    "steps": [
      {
        "text": "Clean the squid: pull the head away from the body, cut the tentacles just below the eyes and discard the eyes and beak. Pull out the clear quill. Set the silvery ink sacs aside in a small bowl.",
        "minutes": null
      },
      {
        "text": "Heat the oil in a pan over medium heat and saute the garlic, onion and tomatoes until the tomatoes are soft.",
        "minutes": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Add the vinegar, soy sauce, water, sugar and pepper and bring to a boil <strong>without stirring</strong>.",
        "minutes": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Add the squid, then squeeze the ink from the sacs into the pan. Simmer just until the squid turns opaque.",
        "minutes": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Add the chili if using, taste and adjust, and serve right away with rice.",
        "minutes": null
      }
    ],
    "tips": "Overcooked squid turns rubbery: keep it to a few minutes, or go past 30 minutes of gentle simmering until it softens again."
